cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  rngrep: hardware-entropy instruction prevalence pipeline and dataset for
  the Rust crate ecosystem
message: >-
  If you use this software or dataset, please cite both the artifact and the
  accompanying paper.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Jason
    name-particle: L.
    family-names: Wright
    affiliation: Idaho State University
    email: jason@thought.net
repository-code: https://github.com/wrigjl/rngrep
abstract: >-
  rngrep statically analyses every non-yanked crate on crates.io for use of
  hardware-entropy instructions -- x86 RDRAND/RDSEED and AArch64 RNDR/RNDRRS --
  classifies each call site by whether the CPUID/feature-detection gate is
  present, runtime, compile-time, or build-config exposed, and computes the
  reverse-dependency closure of the compile-time population. It ships the
  pipeline, the derived dataset, and a corpus manifest pinned to a crates.io
  db-dump snapshot for full reproducibility.
keywords:
  - mining software repositories
  - Rust
  - crates.io
  - hardware entropy
  - RDRAND
  - RNDR
  - static analysis
  - record and replay
license: MIT
